<title>USA: PP&amp;L Pa. 1,090 MW nuke back at full power.</title>
<headline>PP&amp;L Pa. 1,090 MW nuke back at full power.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pennsylvania Power &amp; Light Co's (PP&amp;L) 1,090 megawatt (MW) Susquehanna nuclear power unit 1 in Berwick, Pa. has returned to full service following an outage, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said.</p>
<p>The unit was operating at 100 percent of its capacity as of early Thursday, the NRC said in its daily plant status report.</p>
<p>The unit was idled Oct 28 to repair a leak in a steam drain pipe following a 47-day scheduled refueling and maintenance outage.</p>
<p>The 1,094 MW Susquehanna unit 2 at the same site continued to operate at full output, the NRC said.</p>
<p>--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1627</p>
